{
  "about": "What a batch is: job ads in, the /jobs page's rows out. A DAG (JobBatchName ending in +N) folds by its name alone and takes its root DAGMan job's Owner; any other name folds by Owner and name. Checked by webapi/batches (Go, batches.Group) and by the frontend (groupIntoBatches). Each expected entry lists only the fields both sides compute; batches are in the order groupIntoBatches returns them (largest batchID first); clusterIds are compared sorted ascending; statusCounts omits zero counts; dagNodes is null when absent.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a DAG with a nested sub-DAG folds into one batch, named for the DAG file, id the root DAGMan cluster",
      "ads": [
        {
          "ClusterId": 101,
          "ProcId": 0,
          "Owner": "alice",
          "JobBatchName": "ny50.dag+100",
          "DAGManJobId": 100,
          "DAGNodeName": "A",
          "Cmd": "/home/alice/run.sh",
          "JobStatus": 2,
          "QDate": 1010
        },
        {
          "ClusterId": 100,
          "ProcId": 0,
          "Owner": "alice",
          "JobBatchName": "ny50.dag+100",
          "Cmd": "/usr/bin/condor_dagman",
          "JobStatus": 2,
          "QDate": 1000,
          "DAG_NodesTotal": 10,
          "DAG_NodesDone": 3,
          "DAG_NodesFailed": 1,
          "DAG_NodesQueued": 2
        },
        {
          "ClusterId": 102,
          "ProcId": 0,
          "Owner": "alice",
          "JobBatchName": "ny50.dag+100",
          "DAGManJobId": 100,
          "DAGNodeName": "SUB",
          "Cmd": "/usr/bin/condor_dagman",
          "JobStatus": 2,
          "QDate": 1020,
          "DAG_NodesTotal": 4,
          "DAG_NodesDone": 1
        },
        {
          "ClusterId": 103,
          "ProcId": 0,
          "Owner": "alice",
          "JobBatchName": "ny50.dag+100",
          "DAGManJobId": 102,
          "DAGNodeName": "B",
          "Cmd": "/home/alice/run.sh",
          "JobStatus": 1,
          "QDate": 1030
        },
        {
          "ClusterId": 103,
          "ProcId": 1,
          "Owner": "alice",
          "JobBatchName": "ny50.dag+100",
          "DAGManJobId": 102,
          "DAGNodeName": "B",
          "Cmd": "/home/alice/run.sh",
          "JobStatus": 5,
          "HoldReasonCode": 16,
          "QDate": 1030
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "batchID": 100,
          "name": "ny50.dag",
          "owner": "alice",
          "isDag": true,
          "jobCount": 5,
          "clusterIds": [
            100,
            101,
            102,
            103
          ],
          "submittedUnix": 1000,
          "statusCounts": {
            "running": 3,
            "idle": 1,
            "uploading": 1
          },
          "dagNodes": {
            "total": 10,
            "done": 3,
            "failed": 1,
            "queued": 2
          },
          "selectConstraint": "JobBatchName == \"ny50.dag+100\"",
          "removeConstraint": "JobBatchName == \"ny50.dag+100\" || ClusterId == 100"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a DAG whose nodes run as another user is one batch, owned by its root DAGMan job's owner (without the root, the first owner seen); a plain name two users reuse is still two batches",
